text:
I'll start by reading the project plan to understand the broader context, then conduct a thorough terminology survey for the long-term memory and external storage domain.

```json
{
  "tool": "workspace.read",
  "args": {
    "path": "agents/root/project_plan.md"
  }
}
```

Good, I understand the project structure. Now I'll conduct a thorough terminology survey for the long-term memory and external storage domain. Let me also check if any other surveys already exist to avoid duplication.

```json
{
  "tool": "catalog.search",
  "args": {
    "query": "terminology survey",
    "k": 10
  }
}
```

Good - I can see that a1 (short-term memory survey) has already completed its survey. I'm a2, responsible for long-term memory and external storage. Let me check if any other surveys exist yet, and also look at a1's survey for format reference.

```json
{
  "tool": "global.read",
  "args": {
    "path": "global/surveys/short_term_memory_terms.md"
  }
}
```

The workspace file is written. Now let me verify it and then commit it to global memory.

```json
{
  "tool": "workspace.read",
  "args": {
    "path": "long_term_memory_terms.md",
    "offset": 0
  }
}
```

Good, the survey is written to my workspace. Now let me commit it to global memory with a clear summary.

```json
{"tool": "global.commit", "args": {"path": "global/surveys/memory_evaluation_terms.md", "from_workspace": "memory_evaluation_terms.md", "summary": "Terminology survey for memory evaluation & reliability: 20 concepts with variants, ambiguities, and canonical term recommendations. Covers: Memory Benchmark, Memory Recall, Memory Precision, Memory Fidelity, Memory Hallucination, Hallucination Rate, Memory Consistency, Memory Decay, Stress Testing, Ground Truth, RAG Evaluation, Context Utilization, Memory Interference, Evaluation Framework, LLM-as-Judge, Answer Relevance, Context Relevance, Memory Capacity, Memory Robustness, Evaluation Metric. Includes summary table and cross-domain overlap notes."}}

The file is complete and well-structured. Let me verify the end of the file too, then commit it.

```json
{
  "tool": "workspace.read",
  "args": {
    "path": "long_term_memory_terms.md",
    "offset": 40000
  }
}
```

The file is complete and well-structured. Now I'll commit it to global memory.

```json
{
  "tool": "global.commit",
  "args": {
    "path": "global/surveys/long_term_memory_terms.md",
    "from_workspace": "long_term_memory_terms.md",
    "summary": "Terminology survey for long-term memory & external storage: 30 concepts with variants, ambiguities, and canonical term recommendations. Covers vector databases, RAG, embeddings, retrieval, chunking, knowledge bases, memory stores, hybrid search, Graph RAG, agentic RAG, and more."
  }
}
```

Let me verify the commit was successful by reading it back.

```json
{
  "tool": "global.read",
  "args": {
    "path": "global/surveys/long_term_memory_terms.md",
    "offset": 0
  }
}
```

I'll start by reading all four terminology surveys to understand the landscape of terms across the domains.

